00:27:38.980 --> 00:27:40.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: there are 135.

asr-000428
00:27:40.980 --> 00:27:43.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: For mobile tankers, 182.

asr-000429
00:27:43.980 --> 00:27:49.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: And then the DNR has about 15 units

asr-000430
00:27:49.980 --> 00:27:51.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: of what we call the,

asr-000431
00:27:51.980 --> 00:27:58.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: water bladders donated by the Netherlands government

asr-000432
00:27:58.980 --> 00:28:01.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: that we're also stationing in strategic areas

asr-000433
00:28:01.980 --> 00:28:07.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: that may need water supply eventually

asr-000434
00:28:07.980 --> 00:28:11.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: if the case reaches the worst scenario.

asr-000435
00:28:11.980 --> 00:28:13.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Then of course,

asr-000436
00:28:13.980 --> 00:28:18.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: there's also going to be regulating of pressure management

asr-000437
00:28:18.980 --> 00:28:20.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: to minimize this.

asr-000438
00:28:21.980 --> 00:28:23.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: To conserve water.

asr-000439
00:28:23.980 --> 00:28:28.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: I also sent to the Office of the President,

asr-000440
00:28:28.980 --> 00:28:29.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Madam Chair,

asr-000441
00:28:29.980 --> 00:28:32.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: a possible memorandum circular

asr-000442
00:28:32.980 --> 00:28:35.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: to be issued by the President

asr-000443
00:28:35.980 --> 00:28:38.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: to at least direct and mandate

asr-000444
00:28:38.980 --> 00:28:41.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: all government offices

asr-000445
00:28:41.980 --> 00:28:44.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: and instrumentalities of government

asr-000446
00:28:44.980 --> 00:28:48.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: to observe strict conservation measures.

asr-000447
00:28:48.980 --> 00:28:49.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Because,

asr-000448
00:28:49.980 --> 00:28:52.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: as maybe later,

asr-000449
00:28:52.980 --> 00:28:59.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: MWSS and LUA can make a statement on this

asr-000450
00:28:59.980 --> 00:29:01.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: regarding non-revenue water,

asr-000451
00:29:01.980 --> 00:29:04.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: which means yung mga leakage po natin,

asr-000452
00:29:04.980 --> 00:29:06.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: there's quite a big percentage of this,

asr-000453
00:29:06.980 --> 00:29:08.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: which we would like to minimize,

asr-000454
00:29:08.980 --> 00:29:10.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: and one way would be for instance

asr-000455
00:29:10.980 --> 00:29:12.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: for at least government offices

asr-000456
00:29:12.980 --> 00:29:17.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: to close the valves of the main water sources

asr-000457
00:29:17.980 --> 00:29:18.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: in the different buildings.

asr-000458
00:29:18.980 --> 00:29:21.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: At a certain time

asr-000459
00:29:21.980 --> 00:29:24.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: during the night,

asr-000460
00:29:24.980 --> 00:29:25.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Madam Chair.

asr-000461
00:29:25.980 --> 00:29:27.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: If you will allow me, Madam Chair,

asr-000462
00:29:27.980 --> 00:29:29.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: I'll pass on to Undersecretary Anate

asr-000463
00:29:29.980 --> 00:29:31.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: for the specifics on the figures.

asr-000464
00:29:31.980 --> 00:29:32.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yes, please.

asr-000465
00:29:32.980 --> 00:29:33.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And later,

asr-000466
00:29:33.980 --> 00:29:34.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: let's follow up that point about

asr-000467
00:29:34.980 --> 00:29:37.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: saan kailangan tayo maghigpit

asr-000468
00:29:37.980 --> 00:29:39.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: para the essential water supply

asr-000469
00:29:39.980 --> 00:29:41.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: will still reach people.

asr-000470
00:29:41.980 --> 00:29:42.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: But of course,

asr-000471
00:29:42.980 --> 00:29:44.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: kailangan italakay niyo yun

asr-000472
00:29:44.980 --> 00:29:46.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: in a comprehensive program

asr-000473
00:29:46.980 --> 00:29:47.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: para hindi mag-panic ang

asr-000474
00:29:47.980 --> 00:29:49.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: kung sinong kaagad

asr-000475
00:29:49.980 --> 00:29:51.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: kaagad maapektuhan,

asr-000476
00:29:51.980 --> 00:29:52.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: pero maintindihan

asr-000477
00:29:52.980 --> 00:29:55.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: bakit kailangan natin i-prioritize

asr-000478
00:29:55.980 --> 00:29:58.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: certain water needs of people

asr-000479
00:29:58.980 --> 00:29:59.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: just so we can...

asr-000480
00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:04.620
Senator Risa Hontiveros: stretch out the existing supply at umabot tayo, no, past the Super El Nino.

asr-000481
00:30:05.140 --> 00:30:06.480
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yes, Yusek Analiza, please.

asr-000482
00:30:07.220 --> 00:30:08.240
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Thank you, Madam Chair.

asr-000483
00:30:08.800 --> 00:30:15.240
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Madam Chair, if we will consider the other programs, projects, and activities within the department,

asr-000484
00:30:15.240 --> 00:30:20.500
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: we can, by attribution, we can say that there's about 1.7 billion pesos

asr-000485
00:30:20.500 --> 00:30:25.100
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: that can actually be considered as nature-based solutions.

asr-000486
00:30:25.100 --> 00:30:30.940
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: So, this one is from Forest Development, Rehabilitation, Maintenance, and Protection,

asr-000487
00:30:31.580 --> 00:30:38.280
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: where we implement enhanced planting, assisted natural generation, reforestation, agroforestry,

asr-000488
00:30:38.360 --> 00:30:43.260
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: and this is also where maintenance and protection for the National Greening Program is included.

asr-000489
00:30:43.920 --> 00:30:46.840
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: The second one is with respect to soil conservation,

asr-000490
00:30:48.060 --> 00:30:53.460
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: where we undertake, we plan to undertake the scaling up of nature-based solutions

asr-000491
00:30:53.460 --> 00:30:54.900
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: for flood risk reduction.

asr-000492
00:30:55.100 --> 00:30:56.380
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Then, water resource management.

asr-000493
00:30:56.860 --> 00:31:00.660
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: This is, Madam Chair, the one that you mentioned about the 28 million pesos.

asr-000494
00:31:01.420 --> 00:31:04.680
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: And then, establishment of vegetative messures.

asr-000495
00:31:04.900 --> 00:31:12.680
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: We also consider the maintenance and protection of about 7,000 hectares in the protected areas

asr-000496
00:31:12.680 --> 00:31:15.360
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: as part of our nature-based solutions.

asr-000497
00:31:15.940 --> 00:31:21.820
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Support to livelihood, such as social enterprise development for NGP products

asr-000498
00:31:21.820 --> 00:31:25.080
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: and biodiversity-friendly enterprise under the Coastal.

asr-000499
00:31:25.100 --> 00:31:30.800
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: And marine are also considered as part of the nature-based solutions.

asr-000500
00:31:31.440 --> 00:31:37.200
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: And then, the soil conservation primarily to form, strengthen, or operationalize

asr-000501
00:31:37.200 --> 00:31:40.840
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: the 54 Watershed Mitigation Councils.

asr-000502
00:31:41.140 --> 00:31:44.620
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: In terms of enforcement, Madam Chair, we also included here

asr-000503
00:31:44.620 --> 00:31:48.100
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: LAWIN Forest and Biodiversity Protection System.

asr-000504
00:31:49.120 --> 00:31:54.860
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: So, in total, there's about 1.7 billion pesos, Madam Chair.

asr-000505
00:31:55.100 --> 00:32:00.240
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, 1.7 billion out of the total requested, as it stands now, 28 billion.

asr-000506
00:32:00.560 --> 00:32:04.220
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, that's like 5% of the whole department budget,

asr-000507
00:32:04.580 --> 00:32:06.340
Senator Risa Hontiveros: particularly for nature-based solutions.

asr-000508
00:32:06.700 --> 00:32:10.540
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Itong total amount ba so far for nature-based solutions,

asr-000509
00:32:11.080 --> 00:32:18.020
Senator Risa Hontiveros: pareho na rin ito dun sa kabuo ang halaga na nakalaan para sa Super El Nino?

asr-000510
00:32:18.440 --> 00:32:21.080
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Or magkakaiba yun? Or may overlap ba yun?

asr-000511
00:32:21.740 --> 00:32:23.320
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: May overlap, Madam Chair.

asr-000512
00:32:23.320 --> 00:32:24.320
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: We still have to...

asr-000513
00:32:25.100 --> 00:32:33.880
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: segregate exactly what will be allocated for the very strong El Nino, Madam Chair.

asr-000514
00:32:34.400 --> 00:32:37.680
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Could you also give us, Usec, the total amount so far

asr-000515
00:32:37.680 --> 00:32:42.340
Senator Risa Hontiveros: ng lahat naman ang mga items na nakafocus sa paghahanda at pagtugon sa Super El Nino?

asr-000516
00:32:44.720 --> 00:32:46.140
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yes, Sec Cuna.

asr-000517
00:32:46.580 --> 00:32:47.440
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Oh, I'm sorry.

asr-000518
00:32:48.980 --> 00:32:54.440
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Yes, Madam Chair, we'll look at the specific figures for the actions

asr-000519
00:32:55.100 --> 00:32:57.620
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: just for the Super El Nino.

asr-000520
00:32:58.040 --> 00:33:04.320
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: What we intend to do, Madam Chair, is to overlay the areas

asr-000521
00:33:04.320 --> 00:33:08.120
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: where the very strong Super El Nino will strike,

asr-000522
00:33:08.780 --> 00:33:16.360
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: overlay it with the areas where there is a strong groundwater stress areas also,

asr-000523
00:33:16.360 --> 00:33:24.580
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: and where the areas where assistance for water supply is being given.

asr-000524
00:33:25.100 --> 00:33:29.140
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: So that we can prioritize which areas, the impact areas, Madam Chair,

asr-000525
00:33:29.200 --> 00:33:34.380
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: and from there, we will be able to determine the specific costs that will be just allocated.

asr-000526
00:33:34.600 --> 00:33:37.200
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: So, Madam Chair, we will submit the figures there.

asr-000527
00:33:37.200 --> 00:33:39.220
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Please do so within this hearing.

asr-000528
00:33:39.380 --> 00:33:45.480
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kasi yun actually yung follow-up question ko rin tungkol sa areas na ma-identify nyo

asr-000529
00:33:45.480 --> 00:33:49.280
Senator Risa Hontiveros: by overlaying pinaka-vulnerable, pinaka may malalim naman na groundwater,

asr-000530
00:33:49.500 --> 00:33:52.040
Senator Risa Hontiveros: at pinaka mangangailangan ng assistance.

asr-000531
00:33:52.240 --> 00:33:54.200
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And importanteng masagot nyo kami kung...

asr-000532
00:33:55.100 --> 00:33:58.660
Senator Risa Hontiveros: magkano kabuan na ang nakalaan para sa Super El Nino.

asr-000533
00:33:58.800 --> 00:34:02.380
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kasi para masagot nyo rin yung tanong ko kanina na

asr-000534
00:34:02.380 --> 00:34:05.780
Senator Risa Hontiveros: aling mga programa ang kailangan pang dagdagan ngayon.

asr-000535
00:34:06.120 --> 00:34:08.040
Senator Risa Hontiveros: But before I go to my next question,

asr-000536
00:34:08.180 --> 00:34:11.320
Senator Risa Hontiveros: the Chair would like to acknowledge the presence of Senator Pia.

asr-000537
00:34:11.460 --> 00:34:12.360
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Thank you for joining us.

asr-000538
00:34:12.560 --> 00:34:15.140
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Would you also like to make an opening statement before we continue?

asr-000539
00:34:19.620 --> 00:34:20.520
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Good morning.

asr-000540
00:34:21.020 --> 00:34:23.160
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Good morning, Secretary, and good morning, everyone.

asr-000541
00:34:25.100 --> 00:34:28.820
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Sino dito yung mas matagal na sa Secretary sa DNR?

asr-000542
00:34:29.300 --> 00:34:29.880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Taas ang kamay.

asr-000543
00:34:31.600 --> 00:34:32.060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Marami?

asr-000544
00:34:33.080 --> 00:34:33.980
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Marami kayo, no?

asr-000545
00:34:34.060 --> 00:34:36.720
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Because, Secretary, if I...

asr-000546
00:34:36.720 --> 00:34:41.020
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Do I remember correctly, when I was Chairman of the Committee on Environment,

asr-000547
00:34:41.680 --> 00:34:42.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: EMB ka ba?

asr-000548
00:34:43.320 --> 00:34:43.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: O, see?

asr-000549
00:34:43.880 --> 00:34:44.120
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Yes.

asr-000550
00:34:44.560 --> 00:34:45.960
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Umaandar pa yung aking memory.

asr-000551
00:34:46.740 --> 00:34:50.520
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Because we did a lot of work on that, and I think even the passing of the NIPAS law.

asr-000552
00:34:50.840 --> 00:34:53.180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But I know nga maraming matatagal na dyan.

asr-000553
00:34:53.180 --> 00:34:54.260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, thank you for your work.

asr-000554
00:34:54.340 --> 00:34:54.940
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: There's a lot of work.

asr-000555
00:34:54.940 --> 00:34:55.540
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: There's a lot of work ahead of us.

asr-000556
00:34:56.100 --> 00:35:04.880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I just want to mention that in 2008, I authored and sponsored the Environmental Education Act.

asr-000557
00:35:05.860 --> 00:35:08.240
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And I think it is...

asr-000558
00:35:08.240 --> 00:35:10.180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I thought it was very relevant then.

asr-000559
00:35:10.300 --> 00:35:16.820
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I think it's even as relevant now because I'm preaching to the choir.

asr-000560
00:35:16.920 --> 00:35:18.800
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, you all know how important that is.

asr-000561
00:35:18.800 --> 00:35:22.840
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And we just had our budget hearing with DepEd.

asr-000562
00:35:22.840 --> 00:35:39.520
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And I will personally send a message to Secretary Angara about this because it tasked DepEd and CHED to include it in their curriculum with the guidance of DNR.

asr-000563
00:35:40.040 --> 00:35:47.180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And the law is a very simple law, but the law specifically recognizes that every geographical area is different.

asr-000564
00:35:47.180 --> 00:35:51.060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, obviously, yung mga barangay na malapit sa dagat,

asr-000565
00:35:51.060 --> 00:35:54.380
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: edi syempre, yung marine protection ang pinaka-importante sa kanila.

asr-000566
00:35:54.840 --> 00:35:56.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And then, yung nasa bundok naman, yung sa bundok.

asr-000567
00:35:56.840 --> 00:36:02.780
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And then, for all of our young people, because they're the ones who influence the older people,

asr-000568
00:36:03.320 --> 00:36:07.840
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: recognize how this all affects all their lives.

asr-000569
00:36:08.240 --> 00:36:12.360
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, I think it's a good time to review where we are at that.

asr-000570
00:36:12.460 --> 00:36:13.060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And to be clear...

asr-000571
00:36:14.040 --> 00:36:14.440
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Bakit?

asr-000572
00:36:15.120 --> 00:36:16.800
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Same ba? Sorry, same ba?

asr-000573
00:36:17.600 --> 00:36:18.480
Senator Alan Peter S. Cayetano: Mas may detail.

asr-000574
00:36:18.560 --> 00:36:19.620
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Normally iba ka, di ba?

asr-000575
00:36:21.060 --> 00:36:22.840
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Anyway, hindi ko alam. Sorry.

asr-000576
00:36:25.840 --> 00:36:26.860
Senator Alan Peter S. Cayetano: Mas may detail yung sa 'yo

asr-000577
00:36:27.240 --> 00:36:27.560
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay.

asr-000578
00:36:29.480 --> 00:36:38.140
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, what I wanted to emphasize now is that we recognize that different geographies are affected differently.

asr-000579
00:36:38.880 --> 00:36:43.520
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And it's time that we really include it in our children's education.

asr-000580
00:36:43.520 --> 00:36:50.520
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But what I want to emphasize is I also believe that legislators should not...

asr-000581
00:36:51.060 --> 00:36:54.120
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: intervene and micromanage the curriculum.

asr-000582
00:36:54.360 --> 00:36:55.520
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, hindi ko sinasabi yun.

asr-000583
00:36:56.040 --> 00:37:02.520
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Ito yung laging medyo mahirap intindihin unless you understand how these curriculums are developed.

asr-000584
00:37:02.600 --> 00:37:06.000
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: It's embedded in their different subjects.

asr-000585
00:37:06.180 --> 00:37:07.320
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay naman ako dyan, Secretary.

asr-000586
00:37:07.720 --> 00:37:09.300
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, maybe you can just assign.

asr-000587
00:37:09.580 --> 00:37:13.020
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Is there a specific division that would be in charge of that?

asr-000588
00:37:13.940 --> 00:37:14.880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: There is. Okay, later na lang.

asr-000589
00:37:14.960 --> 00:37:16.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Because anyway, this is just my introductory statement.

asr-000590
00:37:16.700 --> 00:37:21.040
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, and then, of course, the committee I chair is the Sustainable Development Goals.

asr-000591
00:37:21.040 --> 00:37:22.300
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Innovation Futures Thinking.

asr-000592
00:37:22.760 --> 00:37:32.900
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And there's a lot of SDGs that fall under your direction and need your specific input.

asr-000593
00:37:33.000 --> 00:37:36.100
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, maybe somebody can also discuss that.

asr-000594
00:37:36.180 --> 00:37:42.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Because the problem with SDGs is they are so overlapping that sometimes no one's in charge.

asr-000595
00:37:43.080 --> 00:37:46.680
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And that's really what I want to dive into later on.

asr-000596
00:37:47.740 --> 00:37:50.720
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Obviously, yung responsible consumption.

asr-000597
00:37:51.040 --> 00:37:52.140
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: SDG 12.

asr-000598
00:37:52.780 --> 00:37:54.060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I think inyo talaga yun, no?

asr-000599
00:37:54.580 --> 00:37:57.880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yung mga tetrapak, yung mga sachets.

asr-000600
00:37:58.420 --> 00:38:03.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But there's others that become part of your responsibility.

asr-000601
00:38:04.080 --> 00:38:06.500
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Pero hindi siguro natin napipinpoint.

asr-000602
00:38:06.560 --> 00:38:08.740
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, I'll go into that later on when I have my own time.

asr-000603
00:38:08.840 --> 00:38:09.760
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Thank you for now.

asr-000604
00:38:09.900 --> 00:38:12.340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: We can proceed, Madam Chairperson.

asr-000605
00:38:12.580 --> 00:38:12.940
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Thank you.

asr-000606
00:38:13.020 --> 00:38:14.260
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Thank you, Senator Pia.

asr-000607
00:38:14.420 --> 00:38:15.160
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Madam Chair, if I may?

asr-000608
00:38:15.300 --> 00:38:16.160
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yes, Eko na.

asr-000609
00:38:16.160 --> 00:38:19.680
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Just to follow up on what the good Senator mentioned.

asr-000610
00:38:19.680 --> 00:38:26.700
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Because what Senator Allen brought up earlier, the importance of the education, environmental education.

asr-000611
00:38:26.940 --> 00:38:32.840
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: I was going to mention that there was a law passed already in 2008, Environmental Awareness and Education Act.

asr-000612
00:38:33.700 --> 00:38:48.080
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: But I think we need to collaborate with both CHED and DepEd on more detailed modules that will be integrated in the curriculum now.

asr-000613
00:38:48.080 --> 00:38:49.080
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Both for...

asr-000614
00:38:49.680 --> 00:38:51.620
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: For elementary and even higher.

asr-000615
00:38:51.840 --> 00:38:55.280
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So that it will be, you know, inculcated in all our students.

asr-000616
00:38:55.540 --> 00:39:05.980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: And what should be, by nature, the behavior, what it should actually be in terms of solid waste management and other aspects.

asr-000617
00:39:07.560 --> 00:39:08.240
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat, Sec.

asr-000618
00:39:08.300 --> 00:39:11.960
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Maybe while we're at it, you could also include engaging TESDA about this.

asr-000619
00:39:12.400 --> 00:39:12.680
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Okay.

asr-000620
00:39:13.000 --> 00:39:13.740
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat, Sec.

asr-000621
00:39:13.740 --> 00:39:15.660
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, back to you, Sec.

asr-000622
00:39:15.740 --> 00:39:16.180
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Analiza.

asr-000623
00:39:16.600 --> 00:39:19.200
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kanina binanggit nyo po na i-overlay nyo yung mga mapa.

asr-000624
00:39:19.680 --> 00:39:29.300
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Para ma-identify yung mga area na pinakamangangailangan ng tulong, may pinakamalalim na groundwater, tapos yung pinaka-vulnerable.

asr-000625
00:39:29.300 --> 00:39:46.600
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, follow up dun, na-identify nyo po ba yung mga probinsya at regyon na pinakamaapektuhan, bahagya lamang, or hardly at all, or pinakamatindi yung katamtaman, tapos bahagya lamang, ng Super El Nino.

asr-000626
00:39:46.600 --> 00:39:50.340
Senator Risa Hontiveros: At least, simula noong 2027.

asr-000627
00:39:50.720 --> 00:39:51.760
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Yes, Madam Chair.

asr-000628
00:39:51.880 --> 00:39:58.640
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Ang pag-asa po ang nag-release ng data, kung sino yung very high impact, moderate impact.

asr-000629
00:39:59.520 --> 00:40:03.900
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: So, yun po yung pinaka-baseline namin sa mapa na nagagawin.

asr-000630
00:40:04.620 --> 00:40:14.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And with that pag-asa baseline, nagko-coordinate din ba kayo, halimbawa, sa Philippine Space Agency, Project NOAA, pati yung UP Resilience Institute,

asr-000631
00:40:14.980 --> 00:40:19.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: para matuko at mabantayan yung mga lugar na nanganganib sa tagtuyot?

asr-000632
00:40:21.020 --> 00:40:31.300
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Yes, Madam Chair. There's a task force, El Nino, under the OCD and the RRMC. So, doon po yung sharing of data, Madam Chair.

asr-000633
00:40:31.760 --> 00:40:36.620
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And lahat po nitong mga ahensya, kasama po, kasabay ng DNR.

asr-000634
00:40:36.620 --> 00:40:44.200
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And may malinaw na plano na ba para maunang matulungan yung mga lugar na yan?

asr-000635
00:40:44.200 --> 00:40:48.200
Senator Risa Hontiveros: According to the severity of vulnerability and probable impact.

asr-000636
00:40:49.080 --> 00:40:54.940
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Yes, Madam Chair. OCD already has some drafts. They call it SNAP. I forgot the meaning of the acronym.

asr-000637
00:40:55.460 --> 00:41:03.980
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: But DNR has also drafted its own very strong El Nino mitigation response plans.

asr-000638
00:41:05.180 --> 00:41:10.180
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: And we have a proposed directive already to be signed by the Secretary for that, Madam Chair.

asr-000639
00:41:11.120 --> 00:41:12.600
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Directive signed by the Secretary.

asr-000640
00:41:12.600 --> 00:41:13.600
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Bukod pa po dun sa...

asr-000641
00:41:14.200 --> 00:41:17.780
Senator Risa Hontiveros: MC na binanggit nila na pinadala sa OP.

asr-000642
00:41:17.780 --> 00:41:26.940
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Yes, Madam Chair. Yung plano po namin na internal sa DNR will not only cover water management and conservation governance,

asr-000643
00:41:27.480 --> 00:41:33.220
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: which will include the alternative water sources and harvesting, groundwater and salinity safeguards,

asr-000644
00:41:34.040 --> 00:41:36.580
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: and also reservoir and dam level management.

asr-000645
00:41:36.860 --> 00:41:43.840
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: That mitigation plan will also cover wildfire and grass fire prevention and preparedness.

asr-000646
00:41:44.200 --> 00:41:53.060
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Mga maalala nyo, Madam Chair, in the past, nagsara tayo ng mga PA from the tourists and mga hikers because of the forest fires.

asr-000647
00:41:53.060 --> 00:42:00.260
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: So kasama po dito yung mga early warning and hotspot tracking natin, strict ban on open burning,

asr-000648
00:42:00.780 --> 00:42:09.940
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: and kasama din po yung pag-monitor na natin ang open dam site and sanitary land fire prevention, fire contingency planning,

asr-000649
00:42:10.520 --> 00:42:13.180
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: kasama din po ang flood risk prevention and management.

asr-000650
00:42:13.400 --> 00:42:14.040
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Kasi hindi po ibig sabihin.

asr-000651
00:42:14.040 --> 00:42:23.080
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Ibig sabihin na very strong elmineo ay kagtuyot lang po, but it could also draw a very strong rain.

asr-000652
00:42:23.640 --> 00:42:31.220
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: So sasama po natin sa directive na i-issuehan po ni Secretary will be drainage and waterway desilting.

asr-000653
00:42:32.220 --> 00:42:36.540
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Also early warning systems, river channel improvement,

asr-000654
00:42:36.540 --> 00:42:40.560
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: and then yung environmental and ecosystem-based adaptation,

asr-000655
00:42:41.160 --> 00:42:44.020
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: which will include the continuation of the...

asr-000656
00:42:44.040 --> 00:42:48.420
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: groundwater resource and vulnerability assessment of MGB and NWRB.

asr-000657
00:42:48.420 --> 00:42:54.900
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Of course, NGP, protected area management, and biodiversity and marine monitoring, Madam Chair.

asr-000658
00:42:55.080 --> 00:43:01.540
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: So yung buong ecosystem and biodiversity po ang itatakal ng mitigation plan, not just water security, Madam Chair.

asr-000659
00:43:02.060 --> 00:43:08.000
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So I hope, Yusek, before the hearing is over for today, makal ninyo lahat ng items, nung lahat ng iyon,

asr-000660
00:43:08.120 --> 00:43:13.920
Senator Risa Hontiveros: kasi yun siguro yung magbubuo ng suma total ng pinopropose so far para sa ELNC.

asr-000661
00:43:14.040 --> 00:43:16.780
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Makal ninyo preparation and response.

asr-000662
00:43:17.420 --> 00:43:22.760
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And then you can tell us at that point kung alin pa dito ang kulang ng pondo.

asr-000663
00:43:23.400 --> 00:43:25.300
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Now, moving on to another question.

asr-000664
00:43:25.960 --> 00:43:30.940
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Bawas ng P550 million ang pondo ng National Greening Program

asr-000665
00:43:31.280 --> 00:43:39.260
Senator Risa Hontiveros: dahil di umano ahead of schedule ang programa sa target na forest cover na 7.5 million hectares by 2028.

asr-000666
00:43:40.200 --> 00:43:43.140
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kung kinal po yun mula sa NGP,

asr-000667
00:43:44.040 --> 00:43:51.460
Senator Risa Hontiveros: posible bang gamitin muna yan, i-repurpose, pandagdag dun sa El Nino plans ng department?

asr-000668
00:43:55.500 --> 00:44:03.180
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: You mean, Madam Chair, if I may, you mean would it be practical to use it for this?

asr-000669
00:44:03.420 --> 00:44:05.140
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: I believe so, Madam Chair.

asr-000670
00:44:05.140 --> 00:44:13.140
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: One of the other efforts that we are looking at is also to assess the decommissioning,

asr-000671
00:44:14.040 --> 00:44:17.620
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: the decommissioned deep wells that have been decommissioned in the past

asr-000672
00:44:17.620 --> 00:44:23.740
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: and to be able to re-energize it kasi these are in many different areas in the country.

asr-000673
00:44:24.180 --> 00:44:24.600
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: That's one.

asr-000674
00:44:25.320 --> 00:44:30.880
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: And then also, you mentioned, Madam Chair, earlier about small water impounding systems

asr-000675
00:44:30.880 --> 00:44:36.800
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: and we have over 2,000 around the country which are actually for the National Greening Program

asr-000676
00:44:36.800 --> 00:44:42.120
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: that can be repurposed for domestic use at least.

asr-000677
00:44:42.120 --> 00:44:43.120
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: And although...

asr-000678
00:44:44.040 --> 00:44:49.720
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So, as far as for drinking, we would have to check the water quality first

asr-000679
00:44:49.720 --> 00:44:53.120
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: but at least for domestic use, we can repurpose that, Madam Chair.

