asr-001355
01:15:00.000 --> 01:15:13.380
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So this is under the DENR, which is why we have integrated the other water-related offices under this WRMO, namely NWRB.

asr-001344
01:15:00.120 --> 01:15:01.400
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: ...

asr-001356
01:15:13.540 --> 01:15:22.800
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Well, NWRB has been our attached agency since time immemorial, but the LUA and the MWSS, kasama na rin po namin.

asr-001357
01:15:22.800 --> 01:15:30.320
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: But under the WRMO itself, they have some proposed projects also for next year.

asr-001358
01:15:30.520 --> 01:15:34.960
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: But actually, they're existing projects and there are some projects proposed for next year.

asr-001359
01:15:35.040 --> 01:15:39.800
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: These are specifically water filtration program, desalination.

asr-001360
01:15:40.860 --> 01:15:46.340
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: These are small infrastructure, small structures, Madam Chair.

asr-001361
01:15:46.340 --> 01:15:52.120
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Water filtration for fresh water and then refilling stations, water tanks.

asr-001362
01:15:52.120 --> 01:15:54.120
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: For water districts or LGUs.

asr-001363
01:15:54.260 --> 01:16:02.320
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: And then yung geo-resistivity survey, Madam Chair, which is essentially like exploration for more water resources.

asr-001364
01:16:03.360 --> 01:16:05.700
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So there's a budget proposed for this.

asr-001365
01:16:05.840 --> 01:16:12.320
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: It's 223,064,000 total for these different.

asr-001366
01:16:12.420 --> 01:16:17.920
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: There are existing projects already, Madam Chair, which I have actually personally visited a few of them.

asr-001367
01:16:17.920 --> 01:16:20.920
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: And they're very beneficial.

asr-001368
01:16:20.920 --> 01:16:35.720
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Beneficial in the sense that most of these identified areas we chose were those which were very hard to reach or underserved talaga in terms of access to water, Madam Chair.

asr-001369
01:16:36.860 --> 01:16:43.800
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And SEC, itong 223,000,000 para sa lahat ng klase ng mga small water impounding systems na ito.

asr-001370
01:16:43.880 --> 01:16:46.020
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kasama na po ba ito dun sa...

asr-001371
01:16:46.020 --> 01:16:46.760
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Madam Chair, if I may.

asr-001372
01:16:46.880 --> 01:16:47.920
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Hindi ko mga...

asr-001373
01:16:48.460 --> 01:16:49.020
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Hindi ko mga Swiss ito.

asr-001374
01:16:49.080 --> 01:16:49.560
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Sorry.

asr-001375
01:16:49.560 --> 01:16:50.560
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Water filtration program.

asr-001376
01:16:50.920 --> 01:16:51.800
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Programs yung iba.

asr-001377
01:16:53.060 --> 01:16:54.320
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Summer desalination.

asr-001378
01:16:54.480 --> 01:16:55.280
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Yung iba, fresh water.

asr-001379
01:16:55.420 --> 01:16:57.560
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Para lang maging potable to the people.

asr-001380
01:16:57.960 --> 01:16:58.600
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: The access lang.

asr-001381
01:16:58.700 --> 01:17:10.120
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Because many of these are in island communities, island barangays, or really far-flung areas that people have to travel very far to get access to water.

asr-001382
01:17:10.120 --> 01:17:16.460
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So there are certain areas that we pinpointed that we put up these projects, Madam Chair.

asr-001383
01:17:19.560 --> 01:17:20.340
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat, SEC.

asr-001384
01:17:20.920 --> 01:17:32.440
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So before we go on to the MWRO, a question actually na nabanggit din kanina about, I think it was the Secretary, about Manila Water, Maynilad, for example.

asr-001385
01:17:34.440 --> 01:17:43.240
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Paalala lang, SEC or USEC Annalisa, to please prepare the data for the subcommittee on the most vulnerable areas.

asr-001386
01:17:43.760 --> 01:17:47.100
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Most, middling, and least vulnerable to Super El Nino.

asr-001387
01:17:47.920 --> 01:17:50.760
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And kung handa na rin kayo at that point with the...

asr-001388
01:17:50.760 --> 01:17:57.860
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Overlay map para ma-read into the record yung mga areas most vulnerable dun sa Super El Nino.

asr-001389
01:17:58.440 --> 01:18:01.740
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Are you ready already now, USEC Annalisa, or shall, in a bit?

asr-001390
01:18:04.640 --> 01:18:09.800
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Our technical person is not here to show the overlay of the map, but...

asr-001391
01:18:09.800 --> 01:18:12.560
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Babalik ba siya? Darating ba siya later in the hearing?

asr-001392
01:18:13.280 --> 01:18:16.120
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Usually, pag-budget hearing, the technical people are here.

asr-001393
01:18:16.920 --> 01:18:17.820
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Bakit wala?

asr-001394
01:18:18.220 --> 01:18:20.640
Senator Risa Hontiveros: We did that into the mapping.

asr-001395
01:18:20.760 --> 01:18:28.100
Senator Risa Hontiveros: We need the data on the most vulnerable areas, and pag-visual, mas nakakatulong, pati sa subcommittee.

asr-001396
01:18:29.720 --> 01:18:31.740
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, that can be read into the record.

asr-001397
01:18:32.380 --> 01:18:34.040
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Sige, ma'am, we'll wait for that during this hearing.

asr-001398
01:18:34.160 --> 01:18:37.880
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, let's go on to questions to the MWRO.

asr-001399
01:18:40.280 --> 01:18:40.960
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Sino po?

asr-001400
01:18:43.800 --> 01:18:44.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Chief Regulator T.

asr-001401
01:18:45.260 --> 01:18:45.500
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yes.

asr-001402
01:18:45.500 --> 01:18:45.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Okay, sir.

asr-001403
01:18:47.240 --> 01:18:50.600
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, moving from DNR...

asr-001404
01:18:50.760 --> 01:18:58.540
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Ano naman naghahanda para sa Super El Nino, yung mga malalaking water concessionaires ng MWSS, so, Maynilad and Manila Water?

asr-001405
01:18:58.840 --> 01:19:01.280
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: Yes, thank you, Mr. Chairman, Mr. Secretary.

asr-001406
01:19:01.760 --> 01:19:06.620
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: With the MWSSRO actually started preparations and planning for an El Nino last 2022.

asr-001407
01:19:07.000 --> 01:19:13.360
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: We have a presentation here, if you'll allow us to present the significant figures of what we have done.

asr-001408
01:19:13.660 --> 01:19:14.460
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yes, please proceed.

asr-001409
01:19:14.580 --> 01:19:14.880
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: Thank you.

asr-001410
01:19:15.160 --> 01:19:20.160
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: The experience of 2026 provides perhaps the clearest illustration of why continued investment,

asr-001411
01:19:20.760 --> 01:19:24.020
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: innovation, and effective regulation are so important to our water sector.

asr-001412
01:19:24.020 --> 01:19:30.820
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: Last July, Angat Dam reached 150 meters, the lowest level ever recorded.

asr-001413
01:19:31.380 --> 01:19:38.740
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: The previous record low was at 157 meters, a level that would normally result in water service interruptions.

asr-001414
01:19:39.200 --> 01:19:42.840
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: Despite reaching this historic low, we did not experience a water crisis.

asr-001415
01:19:43.340 --> 01:19:44.440
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: This was not by chance.

asr-001416
01:19:44.820 --> 01:19:49.060
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: It was made possible by the timely implementation of critical water projects

asr-001417
01:19:49.060 --> 01:19:50.740
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: combined with operations in the MWRO.

asr-001418
01:19:50.760 --> 01:19:53.840
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: The MWSSRO has made substantial adjustments and mitigating measures undertaken by the concessionaires

asr-001419
01:19:53.840 --> 01:19:57.160
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: in coordination and monitored by the MWSS Regulatory Office.

asr-001420
01:19:57.660 --> 01:20:02.540
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: First, on the supply augmentation, Manila Water has started several projects

asr-001421
01:20:02.540 --> 01:20:08.100
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: and several projects since the 2022 rate rebasing, and several have already been delivered.

asr-001422
01:20:08.240 --> 01:20:15.900
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: This includes the 50 MLD East Bay Phase 1 water treatment plant and the 15 MLD Marikina Portable treatment plant.

asr-001423
01:20:15.900 --> 01:20:20.680
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: We are also maximizing existing facilities, including the optimization of the Cardona,

asr-001424
01:20:20.760 --> 01:20:25.500
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: Water Treatment Plant that sources water from Laguna Lake and the Calauis Treatment Plant

asr-001425
01:20:25.500 --> 01:20:27.900
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: that is sourcing water from the Upper Wawa Dam.

asr-001426
01:20:28.340 --> 01:20:33.980
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: This is the first dam since the 1960s that was delivered for portable water in Metro Manila.

asr-001427
01:20:34.620 --> 01:20:39.680
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: And in the coming months, additional capacity is expected from East Bay Phase 2,

asr-001428
01:20:40.020 --> 01:20:47.080
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: 200 MLD by the month of October, and the Kaisaka Treatment Plant with 220 MLD by November 2026.

asr-001429
01:20:47.080 --> 01:20:50.740
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: These projects demonstrate an important principle, water security,

asr-001430
01:20:50.760 --> 01:20:52.760
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: cannot depend on a single source.

asr-001431
01:20:52.760 --> 01:21:02.660
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: We need multiple sources, multiple treatment facilities, and multiple options that can be activated depending on the actual conditions.

asr-001432
01:21:02.660 --> 01:21:07.000
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: The same approach is being undertaken by Manila in the West Zone.

asr-001433
01:21:07.000 --> 01:21:09.000
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: Next slide, please.

asr-001434
01:21:10.200 --> 01:21:14.200
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: This includes the Anabu, Julian, and Molino Modular Treatment Plants,

asr-001435
01:21:14.200 --> 01:21:18.680
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: which provides additional treatment facilities, particularly in the province of Cavite.

asr-001436
01:21:18.680 --> 01:21:20.660
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: Manila is also developing alternative water treatment plants, which are also being developed in the West Zone.

asr-001437
01:21:20.660 --> 01:21:23.460
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: This includes administrative water sources through its new water projects.

asr-001438
01:21:23.460 --> 01:21:28.840
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: In Paranaque, treated waste water will undergo further treatment to produce

asr-001439
01:21:28.840 --> 01:21:31.720
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: portable water that can be delivered to Manila customers.

asr-001440
01:21:31.720 --> 01:21:37.100
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: This is an important development because it allows us to look beyond traditional raw water sources

asr-001441
01:21:37.100 --> 01:21:42.000
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: and make use of technologies that can provide additional and more resilient sources of supply.

asr-001442
01:21:42.000 --> 01:21:48.060
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: The new water programme will also be expanded through additional facilities in Valenzuela and Pasay in the coming months.

asr-001443
01:21:48.060 --> 01:21:50.040
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: I would like to also raise that this new water supply programme will be expanded in the next two years,

asr-001444
01:21:50.040 --> 01:21:50.580
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: It will be expanded to additional facilities in Valenzuela and Pasay in the coming months.

asr-001445
01:21:50.580 --> 01:21:56.180
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: facility of manila of manila is actually the first in asia to do direct portable resource reuse

asr-001446
01:21:57.300 --> 01:22:01.700
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: so at the same time uh my net is also continuing to optimize its upgrading its

asr-001447
01:22:01.700 --> 01:22:08.020
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: southern treatment plants including potato one two and population to help offset reduced production

asr-001448
01:22:08.020 --> 01:22:12.660
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: from the lamesa treatment plants so our strategy is not simply to find one new source of water

asr-001449
01:22:12.660 --> 01:22:17.300
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: it is to develop several sources and maximize the available option next slide please

asr-001450
01:22:17.300 --> 01:22:26.100
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: next time please second water security is not only about producing more water it's also about

asr-001451
01:22:26.100 --> 01:22:30.580
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: managing the water we already have that is why operational adjustments and effective

asr-001452
01:22:30.580 --> 01:22:35.220
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: regulations become critical both concessionaires are implementing pressure management through

asr-001453
01:22:35.220 --> 01:22:40.340
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: pressure regulating valves and controllers to ensure that available water is distributed as

asr-001454
01:22:40.340 --> 01:22:46.420
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: efficiently and equitably as possible they are also using real-time monitoring and demand projections

asr-001456
01:22:47.300 --> 01:22:49.260
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: of reservoir levels. This allows

asr-001457
01:22:49.260 --> 01:22:51.260
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: them to respond to current demands while maintaining

asr-001458
01:22:51.260 --> 01:22:53.320
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: sufficient storage for the following day.

asr-001459
01:22:54.800 --> 01:22:55.400
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: Third,

asr-001460
01:22:55.980 --> 01:22:56.820
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: non-revenue water.

asr-001461
01:22:57.220 --> 01:22:59.480
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: I think the Madam Chair

asr-001462
01:22:59.480 --> 01:23:01.380
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: was mentioning about non-revenue water.

asr-001463
01:23:01.880 --> 01:23:03.460
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: Non-revenue water is one of the areas

asr-001464
01:23:03.460 --> 01:23:05.300
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: where we can recover water that is

asr-001465
01:23:05.300 --> 01:23:07.060
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: already being produced but is

asr-001466
01:23:07.060 --> 01:23:09.260
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: being lost before it reaches consumers.

asr-001467
01:23:09.780 --> 01:23:11.320
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: For Manila water, the target

asr-001468
01:23:11.320 --> 01:23:13.260
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: is to maintain non-revenue water

asr-001469
01:23:13.260 --> 01:23:15.300
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: below 15%. It is already at

asr-001470
01:23:15.300 --> 01:23:17.180
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: the international level since the

asr-001471
01:23:17.180 --> 01:23:19.020
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: target for international is really

asr-001472
