01:29:35.120 --> 01:29:35.700
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: Water District.

asr-001663
01:29:37.660 --> 01:29:38.940
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Surprising lang na walang

asr-001664
01:29:38.940 --> 01:29:40.680
Senator Risa Hontiveros: uptakers pa.

asr-001665
01:29:42.140 --> 01:29:42.780
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kailangan ba

asr-001666
01:29:42.780 --> 01:29:44.600
Senator Risa Hontiveros: nagdagdag na impormasyon mula sa,

asr-001667
01:29:44.640 --> 01:29:47.200
Senator Risa Hontiveros: sa offices nyo para i-match yung

asr-001668
01:29:47.200 --> 01:29:48.760
Senator Risa Hontiveros: need at saka yung

asr-001669
01:29:48.760 --> 01:29:50.760
Senator Risa Hontiveros: available oversupply?

asr-001670
01:29:51.020 --> 01:29:52.840
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: The issue is really the distance

asr-001671
01:29:52.840 --> 01:29:54.480
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: between the source and the location

asr-001672
01:29:54.480 --> 01:29:56.120
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: because you need to bring the water

asr-001673
01:29:56.120 --> 01:29:58.540
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: to that location. So, it's actually

asr-001674
01:29:58.540 --> 01:29:59.600
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: going to be very expensive.

asr-001675
01:30:00.000 --> 01:30:05.820
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: That's why the majority of the water is being distributed in Rizal because the water source is inside Rizal.

asr-001676
01:30:06.360 --> 01:30:28.140
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Pero doon papasok yung ibang mga pamamaraan na tinalakay nyo kanina, iba't ibang resource persons, including yung mga tankers, para lang i-deliver, i-dugtong yung mga tubig mula sa kung saan may oversupply doon sa mga area na nangangailangan, kung walang malinaw na transfer mechanism.

asr-001677
01:30:28.140 --> 01:30:44.220
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: Tankers are only for emergency use because it's going to be very expensive to deliver water via tanker. We want, actually, our policy is it should be from the tap, to be delivered to your house via the water pipes, if not through tankers because it's going to be too expensive.

asr-001678
01:30:44.640 --> 01:30:58.120
Senator Risa Hontiveros: But we'll be counting on the department and the attached agencies to work something out in this interim ng Super El Nino, at least, habang nilalatag nyo lahat ng infrastructure para from source to tap.

asr-001679
01:30:58.140 --> 01:31:01.260
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, mga kadaloy, mga nakarating yung tubig sa mga bahay.

asr-001680
01:31:01.880 --> 01:31:02.160
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Okay.

asr-001681
01:31:02.360 --> 01:31:04.220
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat po. Yes, Administrator Salonga.

asr-001682
01:31:04.760 --> 01:31:06.200
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Madam Chairman, Mr. Secretary.

asr-001683
01:31:06.760 --> 01:31:14.380
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Yung isa kasing issues, that's why some water districts don't want to necessarily buy from the concessionaires in Metro Manila.

asr-001684
01:31:14.540 --> 01:31:19.000
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Kasi meron pong nakadagdag na surcharge po yun. 25 or 30 percent?

asr-001685
01:31:19.740 --> 01:31:20.660
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: Environmental charge.

asr-001686
01:31:20.760 --> 01:31:23.140
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Yeah. Environmental charge.

asr-001687
01:31:23.140 --> 01:31:27.580
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Meron po kasing surcharge yun. I think 30 percent.

asr-001688
01:31:28.020 --> 01:31:28.120
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: So, I don't know.

asr-001689
01:31:28.140 --> 01:31:30.900
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: So, aside from the bulk water bill, meron kang surcharge.

asr-001690
01:31:31.360 --> 01:31:38.460
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: The water districts, saka yung constituents nila may not be necessarily agreeable with that kind of bulk water rate.

asr-001691
01:31:38.560 --> 01:31:42.180
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Saka hindi nila mapasa kagad sa rates nila kasi ang mahal kagad.

asr-001692
01:31:42.680 --> 01:31:46.000
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: So, that's one issue that I'm trying to resolve with the regulator team.

asr-001693
01:31:47.240 --> 01:31:54.480
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Ang mahal nga kung 30 percent. But if it's an environmental charge, nasa shop ng buong department, diba? At yung agencies ninyo.

asr-001694
01:31:54.900 --> 01:31:57.480
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: Sorry. The environmental charge is basically the...

asr-001695
01:31:57.480 --> 01:32:03.880
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: The charge for maintaining of the watersheds and the wastewater of Manila Water and Maynilad.

asr-001696
01:32:03.880 --> 01:32:12.400
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: So, that's why actually every residential customers of Manila Water and Maynilad are entitled to dislodging services once every five years.

asr-001697
01:32:12.780 --> 01:32:16.760
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: It's not free. It's actually part of your water bill and you are paying for it already.

asr-001698
01:32:16.880 --> 01:32:20.880
MWSS Chief Regulator Patrick Lester Ty: And that is covered by the environmental charge. It also covers for their watershed protection.

asr-001699
01:32:22.380 --> 01:32:22.880
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Well, since...

asr-001700
01:32:23.740 --> 01:32:26.880
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Of course, again, sabi ko kanina, importante yung strategic...

asr-001701
01:32:27.480 --> 01:32:30.520
Senator Risa Hontiveros: The trajectory ng department and mga attached agencies.

asr-001702
01:32:30.680 --> 01:32:34.200
Senator Risa Hontiveros: But meron din po tayong isang urgent focus ngayon, the Super El Nino.

asr-001703
01:32:34.700 --> 01:32:38.720
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, I'm sure the regulatory office has already thought about this.

asr-001704
01:32:38.980 --> 01:32:47.340
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kung ano yung pwedeng arrangements kahit dun sa mga concessionaires para ma-ease ng konti yung pressure sa mga customers nila.

asr-001705
01:32:47.440 --> 01:32:49.160
Senator Risa Hontiveros: At least in the next months.

asr-001706
01:32:49.740 --> 01:32:51.880
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat po, Chief Regulator.

asr-001707
01:32:54.240 --> 01:32:56.880
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Some additional questions sa NWR.

asr-001708
01:32:57.480 --> 01:33:16.820
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Dr. David, paano po ima-manage ng NWRB yung nakaambang pressure tungkol sa pagtaas ng presyo, ng singil or rates ngayong posibleng kumonte yung water supply kumpara sa demand?

asr-001709
01:33:18.720 --> 01:33:20.800
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: Yes, thank you, Madam Chair.

asr-001710
01:33:20.800 --> 01:33:22.060
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: With the permission of the Secretary.

asr-001711
01:33:22.720 --> 01:33:26.120
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: Yun naman pong NWRB is niregulate po yung rates.

asr-001712
01:33:26.400 --> 01:33:27.360
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: But di po natin...

asr-001713
01:33:27.480 --> 01:33:31.000
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: Pwedeng direct ang ikonekta ngayon sa nakaambang El Nino.

asr-001714
01:33:31.560 --> 01:33:41.340
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: But ang focus po ng NWRB ngayon is how to provide, yung anticipate saan po yung magkakaroon ng issue on deficit or possible supply issue.

asr-001715
01:33:41.340 --> 01:33:50.240
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: But focus on how water can be made available to these areas without directly connecting it sa ngayon po, dun sa rates po.

asr-001716
01:33:53.520 --> 01:33:54.560
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Siguro nga po.

asr-001717
01:33:54.720 --> 01:33:57.340
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Pero syempre, nasa isip yun ng mga...

asr-001718
01:33:57.480 --> 01:34:00.660
Senator Risa Hontiveros: constituents nyo at mga consumers ng tubig.

asr-001719
01:34:01.040 --> 01:34:05.260
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Paano magsusurvive na kulang nga yung tubig pero tataas pa yung rate.

asr-001720
01:34:06.080 --> 01:34:13.460
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Parang it's kontra sa dapat na relief na hinahanap nila.

asr-001721
01:34:13.900 --> 01:34:17.940
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kung by ordinary operation of the market, syempre mas konting supply, mas mahal.

asr-001722
01:34:18.040 --> 01:34:20.740
Senator Risa Hontiveros: But double whammy yun sa mga consumers.

asr-001723
01:34:20.880 --> 01:34:23.240
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kaya please keep that question in mind.

asr-001724
01:34:23.240 --> 01:34:25.740
Senator Risa Hontiveros: I-follow up ko sa board ninyo.

asr-001725
01:34:25.740 --> 01:34:28.400
Senator Risa Hontiveros: I'm sure may colleagues sa plenary.

asr-001726
01:34:29.140 --> 01:34:41.200
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And ano po yung ginagawa ng NRWB sa ngayon, NWRB, sa susunod na taon, 2027, para itulak yung pagkakaroon ng bagong water sources?

asr-001727
01:34:41.320 --> 01:34:47.220
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kung mayroon po kayong gustong idagdag sa napag-usapan na at dagdagan din yung utilization ng existing water sources.

asr-001728
01:34:48.900 --> 01:34:50.560
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: Yes, thank you Madam Chair.

asr-001729
01:34:50.560 --> 01:34:55.560
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: Sa ngayon po Madam Chair, we are working with WRMOO on the various...

asr-001730
01:34:55.740 --> 01:35:04.740
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: feasibility studies that were prepared through WRMOO, particularly yung mga development po ng mga new sources.

asr-001731
01:35:05.280 --> 01:35:13.640
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: And likewise, may mga projects po ang NWRB, yung mga water resource assessment ng mga major river basins,

asr-001732
01:35:13.640 --> 01:35:21.360
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: and part of that assessment, yung identification po ng mga possible sources na pwede pong matap,

asr-001733
01:35:21.940 --> 01:35:24.800
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: particularly development ng mga impounding system.

asr-001734
01:35:24.980 --> 01:35:25.640
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: Kasi napaka-importante.

asr-001735
01:35:25.740 --> 01:35:30.620
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: Napaka-importante po sa ngayon, Madam Chair, na maging climate resilient yung mga river basins,

asr-001736
01:35:31.060 --> 01:35:39.400
NWRB Executive Director Sevillo D. David Jr.: and part of the strategy is the development ng mga impounding system that can be a bit more multipurpose po ang beneficial effect po.

asr-001737
01:35:42.260 --> 01:35:55.200
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And nabanggit din nga po kanina yung rainwater catchment facilities, lalo na sa mga LGUs na maraming taon nang mandated to construct and operate those facilities.

asr-001738
01:35:55.740 --> 01:35:56.820
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Mandated by law.

asr-001739
01:35:58.820 --> 01:36:13.800
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Speaking of the WMRO, WMRO is executing a 100 million peso direct grant facility targeting unserved and island water systems via the local water districts.

asr-001740
01:36:14.500 --> 01:36:23.900
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Saan-saan po yan gagawin? At anong mga specific activities at items po ba ang pupondohan ng grant facility na iyon, Administrator Salongka?

asr-001741
01:36:23.900 --> 01:36:24.980
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Madam Chair.

asr-001742
01:36:25.740 --> 01:36:37.240
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: In partnership with the WRMO, we are identifying these water districts na viable or at least qualified to enter into this, to receive these grants.

asr-001743
01:36:37.700 --> 01:36:48.420
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Tinitinan po kasi namin, minsan magbibigay ka doon, wala namang community tatanggap at mag-maintain, lalo na magbumukhang desalination facility po yan, magkakaproblema po tayo.

asr-001744
01:36:48.420 --> 01:36:54.420
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: So baka masayang. So gagawa kami ng criteria, which water districts ang pupwedeng tumanggap.

asr-001745
01:36:55.740 --> 01:37:03.400
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: To maintain and operate these systems. Kasi parang masasayang lang natin kung maglalagay lang tayo ng facility doon at hindi mapapatakbong mabuti.

asr-001746
01:37:05.480 --> 01:37:09.520
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Tinatapos na namin po ni Yusek Rodriguez yung qualifications po niyan.

asr-001747
01:37:10.320 --> 01:37:14.520
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So nasa qualification setting pa lang kayo, hindi nyo pa na-identify yung mga locality?

asr-001748
01:37:14.640 --> 01:37:22.500
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: For, may previous na po, for 2027, lalagyan namin ng qualifications para siguradong magagamit yung mga facilities.

asr-001749
01:37:22.500 --> 01:37:25.600
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So i-update nyo lamang po for next year?

asr-001750
01:37:25.740 --> 01:37:26.200
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yes, Madam Chair.

asr-001751
01:37:26.540 --> 01:37:37.000
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Sa ngayon, ilang mga lugar ang kinalalagyan itong mga island water systems sa local water district?

asr-001752
01:37:37.520 --> 01:37:44.880
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Madam Chair, previously hindi kami privy. Ngayon lang kami magko-coordinate regarding yung matters ng qualifications.

asr-001753
01:37:45.420 --> 01:37:48.800
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: But we will get back to you doon sa nalagyan ng WRMO.

asr-001754
01:37:49.340 --> 01:37:53.600
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Please do. Sino ba dati ang privy sa data na yun? Kung hindi kayo?

asr-001755
01:37:53.600 --> 01:37:55.680
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Si Yusek David.

asr-001756
01:37:55.740 --> 01:38:14.960
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Si Yusek David, the former Yusek. Okay. And then, habang ina-update nyo yung listahan ng saan-saan gagawin ito, may specific activities at items na ba na tukoy nyo na isasama sa grant facility na ito for next year?

asr-001757
01:38:15.960 --> 01:38:22.040
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Madam Chair, since ang targeted niya is island, that could be deep well construction or desalination facilities.

asr-001758
01:38:23.440 --> 01:38:23.960
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Okay.

asr-001759
01:38:25.740 --> 01:38:27.700
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Depende po sa location.

asr-001760
01:38:30.980 --> 01:38:31.540
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Sige.

asr-001761
01:38:31.780 --> 01:38:33.580
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Madam Chair, may may. Madam Chair.

asr-001762
01:38:33.800 --> 01:38:35.660
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yes, Yusek. I mean, Sekuna.

asr-001763
01:38:35.780 --> 01:38:46.820
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Yeah. The existing structures, I went to a few as I mentioned earlier, in relation to what Administrator Joyce Salonga said.

asr-001764
01:38:46.820 --> 01:38:53.080
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So, they're either the barangay or a people's organization, an association in the area.

asr-001765
01:38:53.440 --> 01:38:54.280
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Randy, you know.

asr-001766
01:38:54.600 --> 01:38:55.700
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: And charge a minimum.

asr-001767
01:38:55.740 --> 01:39:04.460
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: A minimal fee just for the maintenance of the area, of the structure, and for the repairs if necessary.

asr-001768
01:39:05.300 --> 01:39:10.600
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Madam Chair, in relation to the map you were mentioning earlier, we are ready to present now.

asr-001769
01:39:10.940 --> 01:39:11.040
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yes.

asr-001770
01:39:11.400 --> 01:39:17.240
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Great. Tamang-tama. Before going on to other concerns with these agencies, please, let's backtrack to that.

asr-001771
01:39:17.240 --> 01:39:25.700
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yung map overlay na ginawa nyo para identify yung three levels of vulnerability and projected

asr-001772
01:39:25.740 --> 01:39:29.200
Senator Risa Hontiveros: impact by the Super El Ni?o,

asr-001773
01:39:29.220 --> 01:39:30.940
Senator Risa Hontiveros: please proceed Yusek, Analisa.

asr-001774
01:39:31.040 --> 01:39:35.800
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Madam Chair, ma'am, may I introduce Ms. Villa Estolero to present the map?

asr-001775
01:39:37.720 --> 01:39:43.020
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Parang presiding officer namin on your mind. Parang I read Estolero. Estolero ba? Escudero?

asr-001776
01:39:43.800 --> 01:39:45.620
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Estolero po, Madam Chair.

asr-001777
01:39:45.780 --> 01:39:48.020
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Okay. So, please proceed, Ms. Villa.

asr-001778
01:39:49.100 --> 01:39:49.900
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Ay, ma'am.

asr-001779
01:39:55.740 --> 01:40:25.720
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: Thank you.

asr-001780
01:40:25.720 --> 01:40:38.140
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: While the map is waiting to be flashed, I will explain the methodology of how the most vulnerable barangays were assessed based on available spatial data.

asr-001781
01:40:38.140 --> 01:40:54.560
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: So first of all, we have three available data when we weighted criteria po ng mga most vulnerable sa drought.

asr-001782
01:40:54.560 --> 01:41:08.740
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: We have the DOST Pag-asa Drought Projections by December 2026 and the Groundwater Stressed Areas from NWRB based on their latest available data of 2025.

asr-001783
01:41:09.600 --> 01:41:22.460
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: And the Water Service Provider Data based on NWRB Listahang Tubig 2025, DILG Subay Bayan, and available WRMO data.

asr-001784
01:41:22.460 --> 01:41:25.760
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: So these three factors were weighted.

asr-001785
01:41:26.500 --> 01:41:32.880
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: So for groundwater stress, there's a score of 1 for groundwater stress and 0 for non-groundwater.

asr-001786
01:41:33.300 --> 01:41:43.400
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: Water service coverage, 1 if there are no water service providers in the area and 0 if it is covered by a water service provider.

asr-001787
01:41:43.400 --> 01:41:49.180
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: And the Pag-asa Drought Outlook based on the classification of DOST Pag-asa.

asr-001788
01:41:49.500 --> 01:41:52.040
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: Drought for 3, dry spell for 2.

asr-001789
01:41:52.460 --> 01:41:54.720
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: Dry condition 1, then not affected 0.

asr-001790
01:41:55.400 --> 01:41:58.340
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: Then the scores were summed to determine the priority category.

asr-001791
01:41:58.340 --> 01:42:01.760
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: So high priority with a total score of greater than 3.

asr-001792
01:42:02.360 --> 01:42:05.760
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: Moderate priority with a total score of equal to 2.

asr-001793
01:42:06.160 --> 01:42:08.340
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: Low priority with a total score of equal to 1.

asr-001794
01:42:08.620 --> 01:42:10.600
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: And not affected with a total score of 0.

asr-001795
01:42:11.260 --> 01:42:16.980
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: So based on the spatial assessment and GIS analysis of the Geospatial Database Office,

asr-001796
01:42:17.620 --> 01:42:21.720
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: we have come up that there are 14,434 barangays.

asr-001797
01:42:22.460 --> 01:42:26.500
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: Or 34% of the barangays nationwide, which are deemed high priority.

asr-001798
01:42:27.040 --> 01:42:32.980
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: But do note that this assessment is indicative only and based on available spatial data.

asr-001799
01:42:33.540 --> 01:42:34.560
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: And that's how we come up.

asr-001800
01:42:34.780 --> 01:42:39.460
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: And for moderate priority, 17,046 barangays, 41%.

asr-001801
01:42:40.300 --> 01:42:43.460
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: Low priority, 9,685, 23%.

asr-001802
01:42:44.020 --> 01:42:48.460
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: And not affected, or 883 barangays, or 2%.

asr-001803
01:42:48.460 --> 01:42:50.460
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: But there is a specific...

asr-001804
01:42:52.460 --> 01:42:58.800
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: Disclaimer that this is based on the drought data of Pag-Asa forecast for December 2026.

asr-001805
01:43:00.340 --> 01:43:02.480
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Thank you so much, Ms. Via.

asr-001806
01:43:02.940 --> 01:43:08.660
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So itong pag-identify niyo unang-una ng 14,000 high priority barangays,

asr-001807
01:43:08.740 --> 01:43:11.420
Senator Risa Hontiveros: or 34% ng mga barangays sa ating bansa.

asr-001808
01:43:12.140 --> 01:43:16.040
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So naka-align na po ba sa mga ito,

asr-001809
01:43:16.040 --> 01:43:22.380
Senator Risa Hontiveros: yung mga Super El Nino preparation and response programs,

asr-001810
01:43:22.460 --> 01:43:26.200
Senator Risa Hontiveros: activities and projects ng department in the budget so far?

asr-001811
01:43:30.340 --> 01:43:34.540
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: For Madam Chair, for that information, we would have to confirm.

asr-001812
01:43:35.000 --> 01:43:41.220
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: But for the available data, we have several projects for WRMO,

asr-001813
01:43:41.220 --> 01:43:51.740
DENR Via Lynelle Estolero: which was overlaid to determine which of these projects directly intersect these most affected areas.

asr-001814
01:43:52.460 --> 01:43:54.380
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And which projects are these?

asr-001815
01:43:54.620 --> 01:44:00.820
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Tapos sapat na po ba yung naka-appropriate na amounts para sa mga projects na ito?

asr-001816
01:44:01.420 --> 01:44:03.300
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Or should I ask WRMO?

asr-001817
01:44:06.440 --> 01:44:07.480
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Thank you, Ms. Via.

asr-001818
01:44:08.060 --> 01:44:09.460
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yes, Usec Rodriguez.

asr-001819
01:44:09.860 --> 01:44:10.100
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yes.

asr-001820
01:44:11.140 --> 01:44:12.980
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Yes, good afternoon, Madam Chair.

asr-001821
01:44:13.300 --> 01:44:14.720
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Good afternoon, Senator Cayetano.

asr-001822
01:44:16.020 --> 01:44:21.080
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Ma'am, if I may backtrack as to the types of projects and how this actually evolved.

asr-001823
01:44:21.080 --> 01:44:52.440
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Ma'am, the projects that were chosen were as early as 2024. And so this is not really geared towards the El Niño. It just so happens there's El Niño now. But that being said, I think whatever projects that are implemented will still apply to future El Niños because the cycle is from two to seven years, though we cannot really predict when they are. So even if certain projects are not implemented, let's say by December this year in order

asr-001849
01:44:52.460 --> 01:44:58.980
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: To address the brunt of the El Nino, which is from January to March and probably even extend.

asr-001850
01:45:00.000 --> 01:45:02.560
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: that for the future El Ninos, we have it there.

asr-001851
01:45:03.660 --> 01:45:12.260
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: So, ma'am, the types of projects that we have would be first in coordination and collaboration with the LUA

asr-001852
01:45:12.260 --> 01:45:16.120
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: is the service coverage expansion of water services.

asr-001853
01:45:16.940 --> 01:45:22.140
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Basically po, ito po yung mga water district na yung kanilang,

asr-001854
01:45:22.140 --> 01:45:33.600
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: because there's a limit as to where their pipes are, to where they distribute their water or source capacity.

asr-001855
01:45:34.160 --> 01:45:37.600
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: So, what we do is we actually grant financial assistance.

asr-001856
01:45:38.000 --> 01:45:49.520
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: For 2027, the total amount allocated would be 124,092,000.

asr-001857
01:45:50.700 --> 01:45:51.940
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Other than this,

asr-001858
01:45:52.140 --> 01:45:55.560
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: we have the development and implementation of water-related projects.

asr-001859
01:45:57.300 --> 01:46:00.440
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Ma'am, if I may, Madam Chair, just to explain,

asr-001860
01:46:00.860 --> 01:46:06.720
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: actually, when it comes to water systems, it's not just water districts.

asr-001861
01:46:07.200 --> 01:46:13.520
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Actually, equally the same number are water systems operated by LGUs.

asr-001862
01:46:13.980 --> 01:46:16.800
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: So, they're both around 500, if I'm not mistaken.

asr-001863
01:46:17.200 --> 01:46:21.960
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: So, the beneficiaries of the projects of the WRMO are both

asr-001864
01:46:22.140 --> 01:46:23.720
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: water districts and LGUs.

asr-001865
01:46:24.260 --> 01:46:29.100
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: So, when it comes to LGUs, the beneficiaries,

asr-001866
01:46:30.460 --> 01:46:34.400
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: initial identified beneficiaries are yung mga remote island barangays

asr-001867
01:46:34.900 --> 01:46:37.900
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: and those other barangays which are considered as isolated.

asr-001868
01:46:38.600 --> 01:46:44.820
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Insofar as water districts are concerned, part of the criteria really is yung water districts po na

asr-001869
01:46:45.220 --> 01:46:46.360
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: plus four, three and four,

asr-001870
01:46:46.460 --> 01:46:46.760
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: oh,

asr-001878
01:46:48.240 --> 01:46:49.200
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: class C and D.

asr-001879
01:46:50.800 --> 01:46:51.820
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: So, the types of

asr-001880
01:46:51.820 --> 01:46:54.020
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: projects,

asr-001881
01:46:54.160 --> 01:46:55.700
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: I think it was mentioned already by the Secretary,

asr-001882
01:46:56.000 --> 01:46:57.580
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: our water filtration program,

asr-001883
01:46:58.040 --> 01:47:00.620
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: which includes desalination or fresh water.

asr-001884
01:47:01.120 --> 01:47:02.420
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: We have water refilling stations,

asr-001885
01:47:02.720 --> 01:47:04.920
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: water tanks for water districts and LGUs,

asr-001886
01:47:05.380 --> 01:47:07.620
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: and yung geo-resistivity survey.

asr-001887
01:47:08.600 --> 01:47:15.300
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: So, the total number of water-related projects that we're looking at the target for 2027

asr-001888
01:47:15.300 --> 01:47:16.980
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: would be 180.

asr-001889
01:47:21.820 --> 01:47:34.320
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Itong 180 projects, addressing both water districts and LGUs, tama po ba?

asr-001890
01:47:35.320 --> 01:47:37.980
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: That's correct, Madam Chair, but mostly water districts.

asr-001891
01:47:38.120 --> 01:47:39.240
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Mostly water districts.

asr-001892
01:47:39.240 --> 01:47:44.440
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And then itong mostly water districts na i-implementahan nyo ng projects,

asr-001893
01:47:45.120 --> 01:47:50.300
Senator Risa Hontiveros: kasama na sila at pati yung LGU-run water systems,

asr-001894
01:47:50.380 --> 01:47:51.800
Senator Risa Hontiveros: kasama na sila dun sa 14.

asr-001895
01:47:51.820 --> 01:47:55.740
Senator Risa Hontiveros: thousand barangays na sinabi ni Ms. Villa na high priority,

asr-001896
01:47:56.160 --> 01:47:58.260
Senator Risa Hontiveros: 34% of our barangays in the country.

asr-001897
01:48:03.280 --> 01:48:09.720
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Ma'am, what actually we're looking at since the final list of the 2027 beneficiaries

asr-001898
01:48:09.720 --> 01:48:12.600
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: have not yet been identified, we will include this.

asr-001899
01:48:12.740 --> 01:48:18.460
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Ma'am, because I think this is also an important map in the sense that

asr-001900
01:48:18.460 --> 01:48:21.460
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: for every El Nino cycle, sila rin po lagi ang tinatamaan.

asr-001901
01:48:21.820 --> 01:48:27.160
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, it's a very important map kasi dun sa sinabi niya,

asr-001902
01:48:27.220 --> 01:48:32.400
Senator Risa Hontiveros: baka itong mga Masbate City, Calapan City, Isabela Cluster, Cagayan Valley,

asr-001903
01:48:32.520 --> 01:48:38.300
Senator Risa Hontiveros: baka chronically naapektuhan ng El Nino, not just this Super El Nino.

asr-001904
01:48:39.540 --> 01:48:40.760
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: Tamag po yun, Madam Chair.

asr-001905
01:48:40.840 --> 01:48:47.520
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: In fact, we've actually seen modelings that they've done of previous El Nino years

asr-001906
01:48:47.520 --> 01:48:49.200
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: na kung saan po nagkaroon ng drought,

asr-001907
01:48:49.200 --> 01:48:51.800
DENR Undersecretary for Special Concerns and Legislative Affairs Ignatius A. Rodriguez: na it always comes back to all the same.

asr-001908
01:48:51.820 --> 01:48:58.240
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And yung follow-up question, sa unang-unang question kanina,

asr-001909
01:48:58.780 --> 01:49:03.520
Senator Risa Hontiveros: so, aling mga programa ang kailangan dagdaga ng pondo sa ngayon

asr-001910
01:49:03.520 --> 01:49:08.120
Senator Risa Hontiveros: in order to address, either to support the 180 projects

asr-001911
01:49:08.120 --> 01:49:17.440
Senator Risa Hontiveros: or to address the LGUs and or, sorry, the water districts and or LGU-run water projects

asr-001912
01:49:17.440 --> 01:49:21.800
Senator Risa Hontiveros: dito sa 34% of barangays, 14,000 barangays.

asr-001913
01:49:21.820 --> 01:49:23.920
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, that is a high priority.

asr-001914
01:49:24.740 --> 01:49:26.500
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yes, Administrator Salonga.

asr-001915
01:49:27.000 --> 01:49:30.360
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Madam Chair, sa experience namin sa LUA,

asr-001916
01:49:30.820 --> 01:49:34.760
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: ang mga dapat nagdaga ng pondo, yung water source development,

asr-001917
01:49:35.580 --> 01:49:40.120
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: NRW recovery, saka yung network expansion po.

asr-001918
01:49:40.420 --> 01:49:43.420
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Yung network expansion po kasi, hagip yan pareho.

asr-001919
01:49:43.780 --> 01:49:46.420
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: You can add more water sources or new piping.

asr-001920
01:49:47.060 --> 01:49:49.540
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Kaya, ganun po yung nakikita.

asr-001921
01:49:49.540 --> 01:49:51.780
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: And it's the same request that we get from,

asr-001922
01:49:51.820 --> 01:49:53.140
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: from water districts.

asr-001923
01:49:53.460 --> 01:49:57.160
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Ang worry lang namin sa LUA, kasi nga, kami nagpapautang kami.

asr-001924
01:49:57.760 --> 01:50:02.700
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: With El Nino, hindi naman lahat ng water districts e-qualified umutang sa amin

asr-001925
01:50:02.700 --> 01:50:04.160
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: or mapapautang po namin.

asr-001926
01:50:04.400 --> 01:50:08.620
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: So, ang hinihingi ng water districts is a direct investment of government.

asr-001927
01:50:08.840 --> 01:50:09.940
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: So, grants po yun.

asr-001928
01:50:10.360 --> 01:50:16.200
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: So, ang pakiusap namin, kung madadagdagan in whatever means possible sa budget,

asr-001929
01:50:16.620 --> 01:50:18.100
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: mabigyan ng subsidy po yun.

asr-001930
01:50:18.100 --> 01:50:20.900
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: And kami naman po, ma-identify naman namin,

asr-001931
01:50:21.020 --> 01:50:21.780
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: kasi nasa amin yung,

asr-001932
01:50:21.820 --> 01:50:22.700
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: lahat ng hiling nila.

asr-001933
01:50:23.220 --> 01:50:26.840
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: And we can give it to the Senate for scrutiny, kung tama.

asr-001934
01:50:27.780 --> 01:50:30.580
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Oo. So, I guess, dun sa paggamit yun ng salitang,

asr-001935
01:50:30.900 --> 01:50:31.940
Senator Risa Hontiveros: kung pwedeng dagdagan,

asr-001936
01:50:32.300 --> 01:50:34.660
Senator Risa Hontiveros: this means, itong tatlong item na in-identify nyo,

asr-001937
01:50:34.760 --> 01:50:38.500
Senator Risa Hontiveros: water source development, NRW, saka network expansion,

asr-001938
01:50:39.100 --> 01:50:40.920
Senator Risa Hontiveros: sa current form ng budget,

asr-001939
01:50:41.080 --> 01:50:42.860
Senator Risa Hontiveros: kulang pa yung items nila.

asr-001940
01:50:44.000 --> 01:50:46.500
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Madam Chair, sa budget po ng LUA,

asr-001941
01:50:47.460 --> 01:50:51.280
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: 29.5 million pesos lang po yung binigay sa amin.

asr-001942
01:50:51.820 --> 01:50:53.780
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Isang water district lang po yun.

asr-001943
01:50:54.700 --> 01:50:57.240
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Mauubos rin yung pera namin sa pagpapautang.

asr-001944
01:50:57.380 --> 01:51:00.180
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Hindi pa namin kayang punuan lahat ng hingi nila.

asr-001945
01:51:00.540 --> 01:51:01.620
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Especially for El Nino.

asr-001946
01:51:01.960 --> 01:51:05.440
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: That's why we're trying to talk to the DPWH.

asr-001947
01:51:05.920 --> 01:51:09.920
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Baka yung hindi pa nagagamit, e malagay para magamit naman ngayon.

asr-001948
01:51:10.400 --> 01:51:12.080
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Kasi yung budget is for next year.

asr-001949
01:51:14.200 --> 01:51:16.800
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yun na nga, may napag-usapan din tayo kanina, no?

asr-001950
01:51:16.860 --> 01:51:19.080
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Item na sa shop ng DPWH.

asr-001951
01:51:20.180 --> 01:51:21.800
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Pero, ah, ayun.

asr-001952
01:51:21.820 --> 01:51:24.820
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Tungkol sa level 1 water supply systems.

asr-001953
01:51:25.740 --> 01:51:31.820
Senator Risa Hontiveros: But that's more a point of coordination rather than ilipat in some way kung ma...

asr-001954
01:51:32.980 --> 01:51:34.160
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Anong tawag nito?

asr-001955
01:51:35.000 --> 01:51:36.480
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Mapahawak nila sa inyo.

asr-001956
01:51:36.580 --> 01:51:38.120
Senator Risa Hontiveros: But that's a different matter pala.

asr-001957
01:51:38.740 --> 01:51:44.220
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So you please submit that as part of the department's wish list,

asr-001958
01:51:44.300 --> 01:51:49.000
Senator Risa Hontiveros: itong tatlo, through the secretary bago yung plenary namin.

asr-001959
01:51:49.000 --> 01:51:50.000
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Unless you're...

asr-001960
01:51:50.620 --> 01:51:51.640
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Nakwenta nyo na.

asr-001961
01:51:51.820 --> 01:51:54.540
Senator Risa Hontiveros: How much more kailangan itong tatlong items na ito?

asr-001962
01:51:54.600 --> 01:51:56.220
LWUA Acting Administrator Jose Moises F. Salonga: Madam Chair, tinanggal na po namin.

asr-001963
